INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'The Living Jedi Testament: proposed foundational manuscript','jedi-testament','I. Awareness: attend to reality before interpreting it. II. Knowledge: seek evidence and remain willing to revise beliefs. III. Compassion: recognize the dignity of others without abandoning boundaries. IV. Discipline: understand emotions and choose actions deliberately. V. Service: contribute without demanding obedience or recognition. VI. Impermanence: accept change and grief without denying their significance. VII. Accountability: repair harm and remain open to criticism.

These seven chapters form an original Knightfall doctrinal outline. The Force may be understood spiritually or symbolically. No interpretation grants authority over another person''s conscience. Study each chapter through reflection, discussion and a voluntary practical commitment.',1 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='jedi-temple' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'The Sovereign Flame: proposed foundational Sith manuscript','sith-sovereign-flame','I. Passion: identify what genuinely matters to you. II. Strength: cultivate competence and resilience. III. Power: develop the capacity to act deliberately. IV. Victory: measure achievement against chosen objectives rather than another person''s humiliation. V. Liberation: examine dependencies and reclaim agency. VI. Shadow: acknowledge contradictions and avoided truths. VII. Responsibility: own the consequences of your choices.

This original Knightfall doctrinal outline interprets Sith-inspired spirituality through self-sovereignty. It does not claim to represent every Sith religious community. Freedom is not a license to deny others their own freedom.',1 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='order-of-the-sith' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Advanced practice: the seven-day guardian journal','jedi-seven-day-journal','Day 1: observe assumptions. Day 2: listen without preparing a rebuttal. Day 3: examine a difficult emotion. Day 4: perform voluntary service. Day 5: study an opposing viewpoint. Day 6: reflect on an error and possible repair. Day 7: review the week and choose a sustainable commitment.

For each day record an observation, interpretation, action and lesson. Keep sensitive entries private. This exercise is optional and adaptable.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='jedi-temple' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Advanced practice: the seven-day sovereignty journal','sith-seven-day-journal','Day 1: identify a chosen ambition. Day 2: examine an inherited expectation. Day 3: practice a useful skill. Day 4: identify a boundary. Day 5: examine an avoided contradiction. Day 6: revise an ineffective strategy. Day 7: assess progress and choose the next achievable objective.

Record intention, action, outcome and revision. Do not confuse self-punishment with discipline. Private reflection need not be disclosed to mentors.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='order-of-the-sith' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Comparative scholarship: Stoicism, Buddhism, Taoism and Nietzsche','force-comparative-scholarship','Compare Stoic judgments and agency through Epictetus''s Discourses; Buddhist teachings on suffering and attachment through the early discourses; Taoist accounts of non-forcing through the Tao Te Ching; and Nietzsche''s self-overcoming through Thus Spoke Zarathustra. These traditions have distinct historical contexts and internal disagreements. Jedi and Sith are not equivalent to any of them.

Research method: identify a primary passage, its translation and context, then explain similarities and differences without claiming direct historical influence. This is a reading guide, not a verified bibliography.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='force-studies' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Proposed observance calendar for both living orders','force-observance-calendar','January: intentions and renewal. April: learning and reflection. July: service and constructive achievement. October: shadow, mortality and remembrance. December: review and recommitment.

Jedi observances emphasize compassion, learning and service; Sith observances emphasize agency, discipline and self-overcoming. Members may adapt dates to their own traditions. No observance requires payment, fasting, dangerous ordeals or attendance. These dates are proposed Knightfall customs, not historical religious holidays.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='force-studies' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Academy examination: guardian foundations','jedi-foundation-exam','Answer in your own words: 1. Distinguish compassion from possessiveness. 2. Explain how emotion can inform judgment without controlling it. 3. Analyze a conflict between loyalty and truth. 4. Distinguish Canon from Legends and personal belief. 5. Describe a voluntary service project and how to evaluate its benefit.

Suggested rubric: understanding, reasoning, source distinction, practical application and openness to revision, each scored 0–4. A proposed passing threshold is 15/20 with no zero criterion. This is a study assessment, not an accredited qualification.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='jedi-temple' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Academy examination: sovereign foundations','sith-foundation-exam','Answer in your own words: 1. Distinguish passion from compulsion. 2. Explain strength without domination. 3. Analyze a conflict between ambition and responsibility. 4. Distinguish fictional Sith doctrine from living interpretations. 5. Define a constructive goal and measurable progress.

Suggested rubric: understanding, reasoning, source distinction, practical application and openness to revision, each scored 0–4. A proposed passing threshold is 15/20 with no zero criterion. This is a study assessment, not an accredited qualification.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='order-of-the-sith' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';